%% alt: Two regions. Users reach a global DNS or load balancer, which sends all traffic to region A, the active region, with its load balancer, app servers and leader database. The leader replicates asynchronously, seconds behind, to a follower database in region B, the passive standby, whose app servers are scaled down. On failover, global routing sends users to region B and its follower is promoted.
%% caption: Active–passive: one region takes all the writes, and the standby trails it by the replication lag, which is the data a failover loses.
flowchart TB
  classDef control fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed,color:#1f1147
  classDef data fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#b45309,color:#3b2405
  classDef standby fill:#f4f4f5,stroke:#a1a1aa,stroke-dasharray:3 3,color:#3f3f46

  users(["Users"])
  global{{"Global DNS or load balancer"}}:::control
  appa["Region A · active<br/>load balancer + app servers"]
  appb["Region B · passive standby<br/>load balancer + app servers,<br/>scaled down"]:::standby
  dba[("Region A<br/>leader database")]:::data
  dbb[("Region B<br/>follower database")]:::data

  users --> global
  global -- "all traffic" --> appa
  global -. "on failover" .-> appb
  appa --> dba
  appb -.-> dbb
  dba -. "async replication, seconds behind" .-> dbb
